          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Surgery and Hippocrates</strong><br>\nWhile Hippocrates is best known for medicine, he also practiced and taught surgery. He promoted cleanliness in surgical procedures, a practice not widely adopted until much later, and developed techniques that reflected an advanced understanding of human anatomy.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Hippocrates's Influence on Modern Medicine</strong><br>\nHippocrates's approaches to diagnosis and treatment have shaped modern medicine. His insistence on systematic study has led to the development of clinical trials and evidence-based medicine, making him a timeless figure in medical history.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Remembering Hippocrates</strong><br>\nDespite living over two millennia ago, Hippocrates's name and contributions are still very much alive in modern discussions and practices of medicine. His influence is evident in the continuing relevance of his ideas and the respect he is given in medical communities worldwide.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
